WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 021. THE CLAIM SOUNDS CERTAIN.. Procurement still needs to know what the evidence can actually support.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
SEPARATE. PROMISE ≠ EVIDENCE. Record the vendor claim separately from the artifact offered to substantiate it.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
TEST. SCOPE · DATE · METHOD · OWNER. Ask whether the evidence covers this product, this use, this version, and this consequence.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
CONTROL. NAME THE FAILURE PATH.. A control is incomplete without an authorized owner, trigger, response, and retained record.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
VERDICT. SUPPORTED · PARTIAL · UNVERIFIED · CONTRADICTED. Nonbinary findings preserve uncertainty and identify the next verification action.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. BUY THE EVIDENCE—NOT THE ADJECTIVE.. A defensible procurement decision keeps claim, proof, control, and recourse inspectable.

